joining me now is congressman eric  swalwell democrat of california and  member of the judiciary committee who is  at the  center of some of these requests  reportedly congressman thanks for coming  back on the show  you found out that the trump doj had  subpoenaed your data  are you allowed to tell us what they got  how much of an invasion of privacy it  was  well it was certainly an invasion of  privacy i still don't know how much  they got you know apple is a little bit  more transparent with its users than  other  providers and so i received an email  from apple it looked like a spam  email that said my uh account  information had been turned over to doj  so we're seeking those answers from doj  right now but the bigger point here meti  is that presidents in our country you  know they set the tone for the country  and so if you have a president who's a  bully a president who has this phony  tough guy persona  that's going to trickle down and so  donald trump  through the years we've seen everyday  americans start to really  treat our health care workers just as  horribly as donald trump would talk  about them  you're seeing nba players having bottles  thrown at them indecency on the  house floor my fear is now that mayors  and governors see that donald trump was  doing this to his  political opponents possibly that maybe  that's what you're going to do now when  you don't like someone who comes to your  city council meeting  and speaks against you you're going to  turn the turn and unleash the local  sheriff  on them that's the real reason here is  that the trickle-down effect  yeah trumpism without trump uh  congressman the investigation is closed  and no  connection was found between your  committee and those alleged leaks  now former trump ag's bill bahr and jeff  sessions have both  denied knowledge of the subpoenas as has  their deputy rod rosenstein  how can that be possible that none of  them knew  uh it's not possible mehdi uh and we  just sent the letter  uh to doj from the house judiciary  committee laying out how we know it's  not possible because  under doj guidelines for members of  congress in a situation like this to  have their data  surveilled the attorney generals the  attorneys general in in this  instance would have to know and i just  don't believe that it was incompetence  and it didn't make its way to them  they know that donald trump routinely  was calling adam schiff  a leaker donald trump routinely was  attacking me on twitter and we happen to  be the only two  on the committee it looks like so far  who were targeted so  yeah i just don't buy it and so i i  guess  um i'm putting the burden on them to  prove to me  that they did not know  i mean the thing is luckily for bar and  sessions they have great reputations for  honesty so  they'll get through this i think uh  congressman on the one hand  it looks a lot like it looks a lot like  the trump justice department may have  crossed some pretty  major lines to try and ferret out  whatever leaks they were searching for  on the other hand i have to point out  that you're a democratic congressman the  obama administration  was also very aggressive in surveilling  journalists from the ap  for example from fox news phone records  etc  uh those journalists among many others  and john brennan  even had to apologize after the cia  surveilled  senate intelligence committee staffers  aren't we kind of  out of lines to cross in this country i  mean obama didn't set  great precedence here i'm sorry to say  many i think that's a good point except  i would distinguish the two and  obama's doj doing that was wrong however  i don't believe there's evidence that  the doj  under president obama was doing it to be  vindictive or that it was politically  motivated it was not a smear and clear  effort  where here we're still learning exactly  what was going on  but it sure smells like a smearing clear  no it's a fair distinction but i think  i'm glad we both agree that it's wrong  whether it's done by a democratic  president or a republican president  we do need to reign in uh surveillance  the surveillance state in this country  and  keep the doj within bounds whether as  you say whether it's barack obama donald  trump or joe biden who's president  and i hope you and your colleagues are  doing that on the committee you created  a flap yesterday congressman when you  revealed that u.s capitol police officer  michael fanon had  apparently been snubbed when trying to  approach  january 6th minimizing congressman  andrew clyde of the gop  have a listen to what fanon said today  i saw him standing outside of an  elevator bay once he got on the elevator  myself and officer dunn accompanied him  on the elevator  and i simply greeted him  extended my hand he stared at me  refused to shake my hand he said that he  didn't know who i was  i introduced myself i said you know my  name is officer michael fanon i'm a d.c  police officer and i fought to defend  the capitol on january 6th  and i explained to him some of the  injuries that i suffered as a result  of that he just stared at me  turned away pulled out his cell phone  looked like he was trying to  record the interaction uh which  ended then we didn't speak and as soon  as the elevator bay doors opened he ran  congressman is it just me or did  democrats get beaten up  and beat themselves up over defund the  police  while republicans are refusing to shake  the hand of capital police  heroes voting to block them from getting  a medal  how is it that your party gets so easily  hammered on police issues and they get  away with that  because we don't punch back hard enough  and i'm punching back is a brother to  two police officers  it's easy to say every other november  that you backed the blue  but when the rubber you know met the  road and  the blue put their lives in front of  ours so that we could flee  and go to a secure location we're really  seeing  who is standing up for the heroes in  this country because right now we're  finding out that to  honor donald trump you have to dishonor  the police  and that's wrong and i hope voters see  that it's been phony for  every election uh before uh now and we  are seeing their true colors and their  true colors are not blue  i have to ask about the lawsuit you  finally serve republican congressman mo  brooks with alleging he helped incite  uh the january 6 riot um congressman  brooks's wife has reportedly sworn out a  warrant for the man who served her at  their home  as far as you know did he do it lawfully  do you think the perp you know for the  purposes of serving the lawsuit  everything was done appropriately by you  and your legal team  yeah my legal team tells me it was done  appropriately medi  but take a step back why was it so hard  to serve  a member of congress why was he ducking  and dodging  service for so long you know he  benefited from the capital being locked  down and visitors weren't able to come  and serve him there but for over a month  and a half he refused to be served  where i come from that's called  consciousness of guilt  well he obviously denies any role in it  even though he is on tape saying some  pretty awful things  uh some pretty things that sound pretty  inciting  um but we'll have to see where your uh  lawsuit goes  uh congressman eric swoll thank you so  much for your time tonight i appreciate  it  hi i'm mehdi hussain thanks for checking  out our channel on youtube you can see  more of the mehdi hassan show  by clicking on any of the videos on this  screen and make sure you subscribe  below to stay up to date on the day's  biggest stories  thank you for watching

